olor: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Swati</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"127\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Shashthi</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"169\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">February 27, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"117\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Saturday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"185\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">10:08 PM - 6:59 AM (Feb 28)</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"125\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Anuradha</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"127\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Ashtami</span></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"169\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">February 28, 2027</span></h3></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"117\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Sunday</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"185\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">6:59 AM - 1:47 PM</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"125\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Anuradha</span></p></td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" colwidth=\"127\"><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Ashtami</span></p></td></tr></table></div><p></p><p></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">2nd February 2027, Tuesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Dwadashi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 5:47 PM - 7:12 AM (Feb 3)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Mangalvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Mula Nakshatra brings transformative energy to this Krishna Dwadashi muhurat, making it a meaningful choice for couples ready to lay a strong foundation and embrace a future of shared growth.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">3rd February 2027, Wednesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Dwadashi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:12 AM - 12:26 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Budhvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Under the blessings of Mula Nakshatra, this Krishna Dwadashi muhurat symbolises fresh beginnings, resilience, and the strength to build a marriage that grows through every stage of life.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">9th February 2027, Tuesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Chaturthi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 3:40 AM - 7:10 AM (Feb 10)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Mangalvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">The serene influence of Uttara Bhadrapada lends this Krishna Chaturthi muhurat emotional depth and stability, encouraging a lifelong partnership rooted in wisdom, patience, and mutual understanding.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">10th February 2027, Wednesday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Chaturthi / Panchami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:10 AM - 2:45 PM / 3:04 AM - 7:09 AM (Feb 11)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Budhvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">With Uttara Bhadrpada gradually giving way to Revati, this Chaturthi Panchami muhurat beautifully blends inner stability with hope and new beginnings, making it well suited for sacred wedding vows.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">11th February 2027, Thursday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Panchami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shuklaa Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:09 AM - 11:30 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Guruvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Revati Nakshatra’s nurturing and protective nature makes this Krishna Panchami muhurat especially auspicious for couples seeking a joyful marriage blessed with harmony, prosperity, and lifelong companionship.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">14th February 2027, Sunday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Navami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 4:46 AM - 7:07 AM (Feb 15)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Ravivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">A beautiful occasion for celebrating love, this Krishna Navami muhurat shines under Rohini Nakshatra, whose gentle and abundant energy symbolises affection, prosperity, and enduring marital happiness.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">15th February 2027, Monday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Navami&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Shukla Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:07 AM - 12:33 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Somvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Guided by the auspicious influence of Rohini Nakshatra, this Krishna Navami muhurat encourages couples to begin married life with warmth, emotional security, and a bond that flourishes with time.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">21st February 2027, Sunday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Pratipada</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 11:27 AM - 1:50 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Ravivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">The presence of Magha Nakshatra graces this Shukla Pratipada muhurat, making it an excellent choice for couples wishing to honour family traditions while embarking on a prosperous new chapter together.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">22nd February 2027, Monday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Dwitiya / Tritiya&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 11:54 AM - 7:02 AM (Feb 23)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Somvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Blessed by Uttara Phalguni, the nakshatra of lasting partnerships and commitment, this Dwitiya-Tritiya muhurat beautifully reflects loyalty, harmony, and the promise of a lifelong union.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">25th February 2027, Thursday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Panchami / Shashthi &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 9:32 AM - 7:00 AM (Feb 26)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Guruvaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Swati Nakshatra’s balanced and independent spirit lends this Panchami-Shashthi muhurat an atmosphere of harmony and adaptability, encouraging a marriage built on mutual respect and shared aspirations.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">26th February 2027, Friday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Shashthi&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 7:00 AM - 10:13 AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Shukravaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Ruled by Venus and illuminated by Swati Nakshatra, this Shukla Shashthi muhurat offers a graceful blend of love, balance, and prosperity, an auspicious setting for beginning a lifelong partnership.</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">27th February 2027, Saturday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Ashtami</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 10:08 PM - 6:59 AM (Feb 28)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Shanivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Anuradha Nakshatra brings its enduring qualities of devotion, friendship, and trust to this Shukla Ashtami muhurat, making it ideal for couples seeking a deeply connected and lasting marriage.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">28th February 2027, Sunday</span></h2><h3><strong>Panchang</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Tithi: Ashtami</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Paksha: Krishna Paksha</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Muhurat Timing: 6:59 AM - 1:47 PM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Vara: Ravivaar</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Closing the month under the steadfast influence of Anuradha Nakshatra, this Shukla Ashtami muhurat celebrates loyalty, emotional harmony, and the strength of a partnership destined to flourish through every season of life.&nbsp;</span></p>",
